  "problem": "Factor ${x}^{4}-{y}^{6}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{y}^{6}={({x}^{2})}^{2}-{({y}^{3})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{({x}^{2})}^{2}-{({y}^{3})}^{2}=({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\n$$",
